<title>JAPAN: Japan brewers say want more EU malt export refunds.</title>
<headline>Japan brewers say want more EU malt export refunds.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese brewers said on Tuesday that they would use cheaper malt from North America unless the European Union increased its refunds on malt exports.</p>
<p>The European Union set a daily refund of 32.50 Ecus per tonne for exports of unroasted malt in the new 1996/97 season last Thursday. The refund is valid for 11 months, including September.</p>
<p>&quot;Our malt import costs rose significantly from last year, partly because of the yen's steep fall. Unless the European Union raises refunds, North American products will be cheaper for us,&quot; a senior official at a major Japanese brewer said.</p>
</text>
